# leet.rule — character substitutions.
#
# Single substitutions first, because a password with every letter substituted
# is far rarer than one with a single a->@. The combined forms at the end cover
# the common pairs rather than the full cross-product, which would multiply the
# wordlist by more than the yield justifies.
:
sa@
sa4
se3
si1
si!
so0
ss$
ss5
st7
sb8
sg9
sa@ se3
sa@ so0
se3 so0
sa@ se3 so0
sa@ se3 si1 so0
sa@ se3 si1 so0 ss$
c sa@
c se3
c sa@ se3 so0
